# Drafted by Gemini (R16 narrator), edited.

~ enter:sk_hills_trail
| Wet beech and hornbeam lean over the trail, while pale mist curls in the hollows. Tiny centipedes skitter across the wagon ruts right under your boots.
| The damp bark of beech and hornbeam crowds the path, and cold mist pools in every low spot. Ribbons of tiny centipedes go hurryin' across the muddy ruts.
once

~ enter:sk_camp
| Rusted rail tracks lead up to the dark timber of the headframe, where green gas curls into the night. The whole camp carries a thick stink of sour sweat and rotten meat.
| Pale green gas leaks around the old headframe and creeps along the rusted rail. You catch the heavy smell of spoiled meat and cold sweat hangin' in the air.
once

~ enter:sk_warehouse
| Smashed shelves and broken stone litter the floor under a thin green haze. Somewhere in the gloom, something lets out a slow, heavy breath.
once

~ enter:sk_machine_shop
| Green gas seeps through the warped boards of the walls. Beneath the sour vapour hangs the heavy, unmistakable stink of a stable and sweating horseflesh.
once

~ enter:sk_upper
| The drift's rotten timbering groans overhead as the dark presses in close. Far off down the tunnel comes the wet, steady chewin' sound of the diggers at work.
| Blackness swallows the lantern light past the bowed, rotten timbering of the drift. Deeper in the earth, you can hear the diggers chewin' through the dark.
once

~ enter:sk_deep
| A thick haze hangs down here, coatin' your tongue like tallow and old copper. When you look straight at the damp walls, the soft earth squirms.
| The heavy mist in this deep drift leaves a foul, greasy coat on your tongue. Look too long at the soft walls and you'll see the mud squirming in the dark.
once

~ examine:sk_headframe
| A heavy timber beam holds an iron winding drum overhead. From its belly, a thick chain hangs straight down into the black.
| The old winding drum sits quiet beneath its crossbeam, with a greased iron chain droppin' out of sight into the pitch dark below.

~ examine:sk_rungs
| Old iron maintenance rungs are driven straight into the shaft wall, thick with rust. They look sturdy enough to offer a way down that does not need the lift.

~ examine:sk_shaft_gas
| Sickly green vapour rises from the mouth of the shaft, warm and sour as an old wound.

~ examine:sk_chain_port
| A narrow gap in the boarding lets the winding chain pass through the wall. It is tight, though plenty big enough for a small body to squeeze through.

~ examine:sk_bed_1
| What looks like a bunk is only a pile of camp rubbish tucked beneath a stiff, smelly horse blanket.

~ examine:sk_notice_a
| A weather-curled quarantine notice is nailed hard to the post. Mayor Somerton's wax seal sits at the bottom, stamped a little crooked.

~ examine:sk_sickbed_a
| A rough pallet lies out in the open air, its coarse blanket stiff with old sweat and damp.

~ examine:sk_bile_bucket
| A dented tin bucket sits by the bed, crusted round the rim with black bile that smells of copper and vinegar.

~ examine:sk_lab_flames
| Dim, bruise-coloured flames lick beneath the glassware, castin' a cold violet sheen without a scrap of honest warmth.

~ examine:sk_sigils_ring
| Crooked sigils are scored into the stone in a wide ring, their grooves packed with damp salt and crushed beetle shell.
